  "verdict": "void",
  "section": "40",
  "quote": "No landlord shall, without legal process, seize a tenant’s property for default in the payment of rent or for the breach of any other obligation of the tenant.",
  "reason": "The clause purports to allow the landlord to seize the tenant's belongings without legal process for rent arrears, which directly conflicts with section 40 of the Act. Under subsection 4 (1), any provision in a tenancy agreement that is inconsistent with the Act is void."
}

